<title>FRANCE: Ten wheat ships expected in Rouen by February 28.</title>
<headline>Ten wheat ships expected in Rouen by February 28.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ten ships are expected in the port of Rouen by February 28 to load around 200,000 tonnes of wheat, port officials said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The destination was not specified, they said.</p>
<p>One ship is currently loading 9,000 tonnes of wheat at Rouen destined for South Africa and another vessel 16,500 tonnes of barley destined for Chile.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
</text>
